{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfpoWz5BYLiaAnJmYDiUj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Worth separating two cases, because they pull in opposite directions.\n\nFor the edge cases I actually flagged, a second model wouldn't help. \"Should `Café` become `cafe` or `caf`?\" isn't a knowledge question — it's a product question about who types into this field and where the slug ends up. Another model would return a confident, plausible answer invented from nothing, and that's worse than an open question, because it looks resolved. The real tiebreaker is whoever owns the requirement.\n\nWhere an outside reviewer does earn its cost: checkable factual claims (does this API actually behave that way, did this change in v18), and large diffs where fresh context catches what the author's context has normalized away. Adversarial verification of a specific claim, not a general second opinion.\n\nThe risk to name explicitly: a second model is not an independent witness. Shared training data means shared blind spots, so agreement is weak evidence — two models can be confidently wrong about Unicode normalization forms in exactly the same way. It tends to manufacture confidence rather than accuracy.\n\nNothing pending on my end right now. If you do land on a rule for when to pull in a second reviewer, tell me and I'll record it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8753,"cache_read_input_tokens":12800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8753},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94565bd7-5556-4c2f-8f21-ee26db32d72c","uuid":"a9332f5c-9c38-44fc-90cd-eb70dfa69cfc","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:53:41.901Z","request_id":"req_011CfpoW